NAME "What the Agent Mode row says when no mode is stored"
WINDOW 100 34
TARGET both

# The question: settings.json carries no `agentMode` key at all. AGY 1.5.7
# changed the unset default from Default to Auto ("Changed the default Agent
# Mode from Default to Auto: sessions with no saved mode, including headless
# -p runs, now start in Auto wherever Auto mode is available..."). So a
# session with nothing stored must start in auto, and `/config`'s row must
# say so.
#
# pigasus resolves the session correctly (setup.DefaultMode() == "auto" when
# the key is absent) but its /config catalogue lists "default" first, and
# DisplayFor maps an absent key to the first value. So the row is expected to
# read "default" while the session is in auto — the panel disagreeing with the
# session it describes.
#
# No SETTINGS directive: the runner's overlay must not inject an `agentMode`,
# or the "absent" case under test is not absent. The runner adds only
# editorMode.
#
# The status row is photographed too, as the cross-check on what the session
# actually resolved to. Note what a bare row means here: it does NOT prove
# the session is in auto. On a host whose terminal sandbox is unavailable the
# binary declines auto ("Auto mode is not available: it needs the OS terminal
# sandbox...") and the same bare row is default's. The /config Agent Mode row
# in the second snapshot is what distinguishes them, which is why this scene
# photographs both.

BOOT_BOTH
WAIT_READY 15s

SNAPSHOT "01_boot_no_mode_stored"

# The panel. `/config` opens on the catalogue; Agent Mode is the first row.
TYPE "/config"
ENTER
WAIT_TEXT "Color Scheme" 20s
SLEEP 600ms
SNAPSHOT "02_config_agent_mode_row"

DIFF
CLEANUP
